WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.125
Step two: a fix, and what it tells you.

2
00:00:03.375 --> 00:00:05.225
Follow the diagram.

3
00:00:05.475 --> 00:00:08.350
At seven thirty, you take two bearings.

4
00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:13.125
A light at three five two true, and a tower at one zero eight true.

5
00:00:13.375 --> 00:00:17.800
Draw each line back from its object, and the fix is where they cross.

6
00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:20.450
Now, where did you expect to be?

7
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:25.025
Half an hour at twelve knots is six miles along zero six eight.

8
00:00:25.275 --> 00:00:27.625
That’s your seven thirty DR.

9
00:00:27.875 --> 00:00:33.075
The fix lies point eight miles from the DR, bearing one six zero true from it.

10
00:00:33.325 --> 00:00:36.100
So the current sets one six zero true.

11
00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:37.900
And the drift?

12
00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:40.525
Point eight miles in half an hour.

13
00:00:41.525 --> 00:00:43.450
One point six knots.

14
00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:46.225
Remember to divide by the time.

15
00:00:46.475 --> 00:00:51.250
So you’re being set south of your track, and if you do nothing, you’ll miss the mark.
